# Build context for the .NET images. The context is the repository root
# (docker-compose sets context: ./..), so every pattern here is written for that
# root.
#
# Patterns without ** are anchored at the context root: a plain "obj/" matched
# only ./obj and left all 18 src/**/obj trees in the context. That is not just
# weight — the cache key of the "COPY src/ src/" layer includes them, so a
# Windows dotnet build or an npm install invalidated the .NET source layer and
# forced a full recompile, and Windows-produced project.assets.json landed
# inside a Linux SDK image, where it is a confusing source of restore failures.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/

# The SPA is built by its own image from its own context (src/DM.Web.Client);
# the backend images never touch it. Excluding the directory outright is what
# keeps the context small — it is 290 MB of the 1.1 GB src/ tree.
src/DM.Web.Client/

test/
docs/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
README.md
